Expected elements: present

The single weakest element is the prose block of the `Data` row in the Transaction pane — the eight lines beginning "Every block, transaction, address and hash on this chain…", directly beneath the `Synthetic demo data` badge.

It is the weakest because it is simultaneously the most important content on the page and the worst-set text on it. It is right-aligned: eight lines flush right and ragged on the left edge the eye returns to on every line — the only paragraph set that way in the whole product, and demonstrably not a decision, because the two lesser paragraphs lower in the very same pane (`EXECUTIONS`, `DECODED INPUT`) are set left. It reads as prose that fell into a value column and inherited its alignment.

And the move did not buy what it was made to buy. The band cost ~190 px of viewport; this row occupies roughly 230 px of a ~1000 px pane — about 23% — so the cost was relocated and grown, not reclaimed, and it now pushes the pane's actual chain data down until `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` is clipped at the viewport bottom. The row is not too quiet for its claim. It is too loud and too badly set, in the one pane whose job is fields.

Left-aligned at full pane width the same sentences are four or five lines and the fields return above the fold. Nothing about the wording needs to change.

